r services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 29.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.5, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.7 to 4.5. December accounts for 3% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 2% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 84 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,765 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows a pattern of contracts just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices could be standard, budgets fixed, or needs separate. Statistical trends don't indicate improper actions by the body or contractors.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for unusual patterns. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same need. Look at contract [1] to see what was purchased and if it aligns with the body's stated goals.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["pV9YyuLXK6IkJPJS%2BPS9vg%3D%3D","%2Bx8cqKYnogYkJPJS%2BPS9vg%3D%3D","ZWOiKldWvbK8ebB%2FXTwy0A%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}